## 14. Decision Outcome

**Proposed:** Use a Saga Pattern coordinated by the Order Management Service to manage order, payment, and inventory workflows.

Each service will maintain its own authoritative state and perform local transactions. Domain events will communicate completed state changes, while explicit commands will request operations. Failed workflows will use idempotent compensating actions and persistent recovery tracking.

The detailed order state machine, payment capture policy, inventory commitment timing, reservation expiry, and compensation rules must be finalized before production implementation.

